    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d523">

                <pb facs="0693" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/6–2647: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-06-26">June 26, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>170. Number Zurc 834. Thirty-fifth meeting of Joint Commission held afternoon 25
                    June at the Capitol Building, Seoul. General Shtikov chairman. In attendance
                    were about 425 designated representatives of the political parties and social
                    organizations of South Korea plus about 200 invited guests and the press.
                    Appropriate music was furnished by the Seoul Symphony Orchestra. General Brown
                    made speech informing representatives of the purpose and procedure of
                        consultation.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d523-f1"/> Following the speech the
                    delegation shook hands with all representatives. Much cordiality between the
                    Soviets and a large number of the Korean representatives was evident. Copies of
                    speech being airmailed to Plans and Operations Division War Department with
                    request copy be furnished State Dept.</p>
                <p>Deadline for submission of answers to questionnaires has been changed to 5 July
                    and beginning of oral consultation 7 July. Soviet delegation depart for North
                    Korea today leaving Mr. Tounkin to continue work in Subcommission No. One on
                    final list of organizations to participate in consultation. US delegation will
                    depart for North Korea 29 June. Results of analysis of political orientation of
                    organizations and effect on US position will be sent in later radio.<anchor
                        n="9" xml:id="d523-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacobs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d523-f1" n="8" xml:id="d523-f1-content">
                <p>For text of statement by General Brown on June 25 and by General Shtikov on June
                    30, see <hi rendition="#italic">Korea’s Independence</hi>, p. 45.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d523-f2" n="9" xml:id="d523-f2-content">
